      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "\u2022Metastatic disease should be considered in cervical cancer patients presenting with eye pain and vision complaints.\u2022Distant metastasis involving less common organ sites, such as the eye, suggest a poor prognosis with short life expectancy.\u2022In cases of cervical cancer metastatic to the eye, radiotherapy may decrease the incidence of retinal detachment and vision loss."},
